  "goodToKnow": "Die Industrialisierung is industrialisation. In Germany it took off around 1835, when the first railway ran from Nuremberg to Fürth, and accelerated after 1871 with coal and steel in the Ruhr and chemicals and electrical engineering. Poverty among workers created the soziale Frage, which led to Bismarck's social insurance laws in the 1880s. It has no plural."
